    </p>

    <h2>2. What Panda is — and is not</h2>
    <p>
      Panda is a record-keeping, planning, and informational tool for
      smallholder horticulture farmers. It is <strong>not</strong> a substitute
      for professional agronomy advice, a licensed agro-dealer's product
      guidance, a veterinarian, or a financial / tax adviser. The disease
      detection feature returns photo-based estimates; any treatment
      recommendation must be verified against KEPHIS and PCPB registration,
      withholding periods, and dosage guidance with a licensed dealer before
      application. Market prices are aggregated from public sources (NAFIS,
      county boards) and may be 1–3 days delayed; verify the price with the
      buyer before transacting.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Eligibility &amp; accounts</h2>
    <p>
